refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public StreamPollHandle::__construct resourcestream
Creates a handle that allows stream to be watched by an Io\Poll\Context. The handle holds a reference to the stream, which therefore stays open until fclose is called on it.

&reftitle.parameters;
stream
An open stream, such as a socket created with stream_socket_client or stream_socket_accept.

&reftitle.errors;

 Throws a TypeError if
 stream is not an open stream.

  &reftitle.examples;

   StreamPollHandle::__construct example


<?php
use Io\Poll\Context;
use Io\Poll\Event;

[$reader, $writer] = stream_socket_pair(STREAM_PF_UNIX, STREAM_SOCK_STREAM, STREAM_IPPROTO_IP);

$handle = new StreamPollHandle($reader);

$context = new Context();
$watcher = $context->add($handle, [Event::Read]);
var_dump($watcher->isActive());


   &example.outputs;


bool(true)
